WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.378
♪ 

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:09.175
♪ 

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:12.554
♪ 

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:16.891
♪ 

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:20.270
Yeah, you can see that, uh,

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:21.855
something just came down
through here,

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:25.859
all this lichen's
all rubbed off.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.112
Could be, probably more than
likely an old slide,

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:31.698
maybe a bear come down
through here.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.993
Never know. Not seeing
any tracks or signs.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:39.622
So I don't think anything's real
fresh, but they are using this.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:42.667
It is hunting season,

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:47.505
we have a very long deer season
on the island,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.965
which is a blessing.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.550
We don't have moose
on this island,

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:55.597
we don't have really anything
else besides black-tail deer.

00:00:55.638 --> 00:01:01.144
Earlier in the spring I did see
a lot of game trails and tracks,

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:06.149
and it looks like it could be
at some time very profitable.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:12.072
♪ 

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:14.657
(game call squeaks)

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.787
(squeak)

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:21.790
♪ 

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:24.042
(squeak)

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:29.089
♪ 

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:35.011
♪ 

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:39.641
I know this call works good
for, for bear, for sure.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:42.560
Um, in the spring when
the fawns are dropping,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:46.523
you can tighten these bands
and make a fawn call,

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:48.525
and then bears will beeline
right for you.

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:51.152
They'll run you smooth over

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:52.570
looking for that fawn.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.405
It's, uh...

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.200
So, so far it's worked on bears.

00:01:57.242 --> 00:02:00.537
Hopefully she'll get,
we'll get a deer in here.

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:06.709
We do have a predator issue
on this island.

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:10.505
In the spring, those black bear,
when the fawns start dropping,

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:14.676
their only thing
is eating fawns.

00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:18.888
And the wolves, their only thing
is eating these black-tail deer.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.519
Our deer population
is dwindling.

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:28.898
It really hammers our chance
to feed our family

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:32.277
when the predator population
is so high

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.071
that you're not seeing the deer.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:39.701
♪ 

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.077
Wind's really kicking up.

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:45.957
I see these conked-up
hemlocks here,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.250
means they're really rotten

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.919
and they're starting
to rock and roll.

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:53.840
♪ 

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:58.219
You got to watch, too, grabbing
these little rotten ones.

00:02:58.261 --> 00:03:01.806
You shake 'em
and that top just wobbles.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:05.476
Sucker will come off there
and whack you right in the bean.

00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:09.689
When I first came up logging,
a buddy of mine,

00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:14.569
he was cutting, and you can see
there's a rotten limb

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:16.946
that had already
broke off there.

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:20.575
And right above that
big sweeper, it comes out,

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:23.953
he was cutting on it
and started pounding ledges.

00:03:23.953 --> 00:03:26.039
Well, it was rotten
like that bottom one,

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.292
and that whole sweeper come off
and crushed him.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:32.420
Killed him, killed him on site.

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:36.341
♪ 

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:40.094
I do miss logging
and I do miss cutting.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:43.139
But it is nice to know
every day I'm home with the kids

00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:47.143
and I'm not coming home
in a box either.

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:49.187
Happens to a lot of us.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:53.316
♪ 

